{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (scvi_n200, multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.678 vs config_019 (pca_n2000, same other settings) at 0.639, a +0.039 gain. However, we cannot yet tell whether scvi_n200 improves the RNA representation in general or only benefits from richer interaction with image features during fusion. Question: Does scvi_n200 outperform pca_n2000 in the RNA-only multiprofile setting? Config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002 (same but pca_n2000, acc=0.591). If scvi_n200 also lifts RNA-only performance, the gain is in the RNA representation itself and we should expect similar improvements when upgrading the image encoder next. If it does not, the scvi benefit is fusion-specific, redirecting our strategy toward image-side improvements. This is the best use of the next experiment because it isolates one critical design axis (RNA encoder quality) with a controlled comparison, reducing uncertainty that directly informs whether to prioritize RNA or image encoder upgrades in subsequent trials."
}

